  "description": "<p>ocfl-java-client v2.2.1 supports range requests at the ocfl level. Once fcrepo us updated to this version, we should see if we can make use of this in fedora in order to only retrieve the parts of the file that a user is requesting, then they make a request with an HTTP Range header.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/OCFL/ocfl-java/issues/118\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/OCFL/ocfl-java/issues/118</a> </p>",
